IMPORT prelude

-- Government Procurement Act 1997 (Singapore) -- who may challenge a covered government procurement, and how (ss 2, 7(2), 7(3)),
-- the 15-day window, fee, deposit and service (ss 12, 13), notice of hearing (s 14), when a challenge must be declared invalid
-- (s 15(2)), suspending the tender (s 16(1), (3), (7)), the breach the applicant may rely on (s 17(2)), the 45-day determination
-- (s 18(1), (2)), the remedies the Tribunal may give (s 18(3), (5)), certified copies within 7 days (s 19(2)), the 3-year
-- retention of documents (s 24), and procurements initiated before 13 May 2002 (s 26).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GPA1997.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in
-- the body is 40/2019 (ss 8(6), 21(2)). The retrieval record calls it the "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0114 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to -- here, a supplier
-- bidding for a government contract. No scenario has asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the supplier's challenge.
-- Not encoded: which States, contracting authorities and procurements are covered (ss 3, 4 -- all by Gazette order, none
-- retrieved), the Minister's certificates beyond their effect (s 5), the procurement regulations themselves (s 6 -- not
-- retrieved, so no breach of them can be tested here), the Tribunal's constitution, appointments and powers (ss 8 to 11, 22),
-- costs beyond the deposit arithmetic (s 21), enforcement (s 20), reporting to the Minister (s 23), and the prescribed fee and
-- deposit amounts (s 25 regulations, not retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive rows (the writing-l4-rules
-- skill was not loadable in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Government Procurement Act 1997 -- challenges`

§§ `2 and 7(2) -- to whom the duty is owed`

-- s 2 "relevant supplier" (and, in the same words, "relevant Protocol supplier"), in relation to a procurement subject to the Act:
-- "(a) a supplier who is a national of Singapore or of a relevant State that is specified in an order made under section 4(2) as
-- one to which that procurement relates; (b) a supplier which is a company or an association or a body of persons ... which is
-- formed under the laws of Singapore or such relevant State and has its principal place of business in Singapore or such
-- relevant State; or (c) a supplier ... specified under that order".
-- s 7(1): a contracting authority "must, in undertaking a procurement subject to the Act, comply with the regulations made under
-- section 6". (2): the duty "is a duty owed to -- (a) relevant suppliers or relevant Protocol suppliers in relation to that
-- procurement; and (b) such other supplier or class of suppliers as the Minister may, by order published in the Gazette, declare."
--
-- Reading of (b): BOTH limbs are required -- formed under the laws of Singapore or a specified State, AND principal place of
-- business in Singapore or a specified State. Whether a body formed in one and based in the other qualifies is read here as yes
-- ("Singapore or such relevant State" in each limb); that is an inference from the wording.
DECLARE Supplier HAS
    `a national of Singapore or of a specified State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `formed under the laws of Singapore or of a specified State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `principal place of business in Singapore or a specified State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specified as a relevant supplier in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared by the Minister under section 7(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the supplier` IS A Supplier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplier is a relevant supplier` IF
        `the supplier`'s `a national of Singapore or of a specified State`
    OR  (    `the supplier`'s `formed under the laws of Singapore or of a specified State`
         AND `the supplier`'s `principal place of business in Singapore or a specified State`)
    OR  `the supplier`'s `specified as a relevant supplier in the order`

GIVEN `the supplier` IS A Supplier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty is owed to the supplier` IF
        `the supplier is a relevant supplier` `the supplier`
    OR  `the supplier`'s `declared by the Minister under section 7(2)(b)`

§§ `7(3) -- the Tribunal, not the courts`

-- s 7(3): "A breach of a duty referred to in subsection (1) is not to be the subject of any proceedings in any court but may be
-- the subject of a challenge brought before the Tribunal by a supplier to whom the duty is owed and who has suffered, or
-- reasonably risks suffering, loss or damage as a result of the breach."
-- s 2 "supplier": "a person who sought, or who seeks, or who would have wished, to be the person to whom a contract of
-- procurement, being a procurement subject to the Act, is awarded" -- so a would-be bidder who never bid is still a supplier.
DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the Tribunal`
    `no forum under this Act`

GIVEN `the supplier` IS A Supplier, `procurement subject to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `suffered loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonably risks loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Forum
`where the breach may be challenged` MEANS
    IF      `procurement subject to the Act`
        AND `the duty is owed to the supplier` `the supplier`
        AND (`suffered loss or damage` OR `reasonably risks loss or damage`)
    THEN `the Tribunal`
    ELSE `no forum under this Act`

§§ `12 and 13 -- lodging the challenge`

-- s 12(1): the applicant "must, within 15 days from the date the facts constituting the basis of the challenge first took
-- place -- (a) lodge with the Registrar a notice of challenge ...; (b) pay the Registrar the fee prescribed (if any) ...; and
-- (c) serve a copy of the Notice of Challenge on the contracting authority".
-- Counting: day 0 is the day the facts first took place, and "within 15 days" is read as at most 15 days after it. That is an
-- inference; the Act does not say how the days are counted.
-- s 13(1): the deposit is paid "at the time the Notice of Challenge is lodged"; (2) "The challenge is deemed to have been
-- withdrawn if the applicant fails to comply with subsection (1)."
GIVEN `days after the facts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the challenge is within the 15 days` IF
    `days after the facts` AT MOST 15

GIVEN `deposit paid on lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the challenge is deemed withdrawn` IF
    NOT `deposit paid on lodgment`

-- s 13(3): the deposit "is to be used by the Registrar to pay any costs awarded by the Tribunal to the contracting authority";
-- (4) if insufficient, the authority "may recover the balance of the costs in the manner referred to in section 21"; (5) after
-- disposal, if there is no outstanding claim for costs, the Registrar "must ... release the deposit or the balance of the deposit".
GIVEN `the deposit` IS A NUMBER, `costs awarded to the authority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deposit released to the applicant` MEANS
    IF `costs awarded to the authority` AT LEAST `the deposit` THEN 0
    ELSE `the deposit` MINUS `costs awarded to the authority`

GIVEN `the deposit` IS A NUMBER, `costs awarded to the authority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the costs still recoverable from the applicant` MEANS
    IF `costs awarded to the authority` AT MOST `the deposit` THEN 0
    ELSE `costs awarded to the authority` MINUS `the deposit`

§§ `14 -- notice of the hearing`

-- s 14(c): the Registrar must "give 14 days' notice of the hearing to the applicant and the contracting authority concerned".
GIVEN `days of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice of hearing is enough` IF
    `days of notice` AT LEAST 14

§§ `15(2) and 26 -- when the challenge must be declared invalid`

-- s 26(1): "This Act does not apply to or affect any procurement which has been initiated before 13 May 2002." (2) It is deemed
-- initiated if "(a) the invitation to tender ... has been issued; (b) the qualification of suppliers, being a qualification of
-- suppliers undertaken solely for that particular procurement, has commenced; or (c) in a case where no tender is to be called
-- ..., the contracting authority concerned had communicated with a potential supplier with a view to the making or obtaining of
-- an offer".
GIVEN `tender invited before 13 May 2002` IS A BOOLEAN, `dedicated qualification begun before 13 May 2002` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `no tender and supplier approached before 13 May 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the procurement was initiated before 13 May 2002` IF
        `tender invited before 13 May 2002`
    OR  `dedicated qualification begun before 13 May 2002`
    OR  `no tender and supplier approached before 13 May 2002`

-- s 15(2): "the Tribunal must declare a challenge invalid if -- (a) the procurement ... is not a procurement subject to the Act;
-- (b) the regulation ... alleged to have [been] breached is inapplicable to the procurement ...; (c) [it] is inapplicable, by
-- virtue of an order made under section 4 ...; (d) the procurement ... has been initiated before 13 May 2002 ...; (e) the
-- applicant is not a supplier entitled to bring a challenge under section 7(3); (f) the applicant did not lodge or serve the
-- Notice of Challenge within the time prescribed by section 12(1), unless the Tribunal is satisfied that there has been no
-- unreasonable delay on the part of the applicant; or (g) the Notice of Challenge does not comply with section 12(2)."
-- (3): for (f) the Tribunal "must take into account the date the applicant became aware, or ought reasonably to have become
-- aware" of the facts. (4): breach of a condition then imposed means it "may" declare the challenge invalid -- not modelled.
DECLARE Challenge HAS
    `procurement subject to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulation applies to the procurement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulation excluded by a section 4 order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `initiated before 13 May 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applicant entitled under section 7(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the facts to lodgment and service` IS A NUMBER
    `Tribunal satisfied there was no unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the challenge` IS A Challenge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the challenge must be declared invalid` IF
        (NOT `the challenge`'s `procurement subject to the Act`)
    OR  (NOT `the challenge`'s `regulation applies to the procurement`)
    OR  `the challenge`'s `regulation excluded by a section 4 order`
    OR  `the challenge`'s `initiated before 13 May 2002`
    OR  (NOT `the challenge`'s `applicant entitled under section 7(3)`)
    OR  (    (NOT `the challenge is within the 15 days` (`the challenge`'s `days after the facts to lodgment and service`))
         AND (NOT `the challenge`'s `Tribunal satisfied there was no unreasonable delay`))
    OR  (NOT `the challenge`'s `notice in the prescribed form`)

§§ `16 -- suspending the procurement`

-- s 16(1): the applicant may apply for a suspension "at any time after the applicant has -- (a) lodged the Notice of Challenge
-- ...; (b) paid the fee ... and the deposit ...; and (c) served the Notice of Challenge". (3): "The Tribunal must not make an
-- order under this section if -- (a) such suspension is against the public interest; or (b) the contract ... has already been
-- awarded at the date of hearing of the application". (8): a Minister's certificate that suspension is against the public
-- interest is "conclusive evidence". (7): the Tribunal "must rescind the order if the continuance of such suspension is against
-- the public interest."
DECLARE SuspensionApplication HAS
    `notice lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fee and deposit paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `suspension against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Minister certified against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contract awarded by the hearing date` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS A SuspensionApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may suspend the procurement` IF
        `the application`'s `notice lodged`
    AND `the application`'s `fee and deposit paid`
    AND `the application`'s `notice served`
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `suspension against the public interest`)
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `Minister certified against the public interest`)
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `contract awarded by the hearing date`)

GIVEN `continuance against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister certified continuance against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal must rescind the suspension` IF
    `continuance against the public interest` OR `Minister certified continuance against the public interest`

§§ `17(2) -- the breach the applicant may rely on`

-- s 17(1): "The onus of proving the breach of duty ... is on the applicant." (2): "Except with the consent of the Tribunal ...
-- the applicant may not, at the hearing of the challenge, rely on any breach of duty other than that identified in the Notice of
-- Challenge."
GIVEN `identified in the Notice of Challenge` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Tribunal consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant may rely on the breach` IF
    `identified in the Notice of Challenge` OR `the Tribunal consents`

§§ `18(1), (2) and 19(2) -- time for the determination`

-- s 18(1): "The Tribunal must issue its determination on a challenge within 45 days from the date of lodgment of the Notice of
-- Challenge by the applicant unless there are exceptional circumstances justifying an extension of time." (2): "Subsection (1)
-- does not apply if the challenge has been disposed of under section 15." Same day-counting inference as s 12.
GIVEN `days after lodgment` IS A NUMBER, `exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN, `disposed of under section 15` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the determination is out of time` IF
        `days after lodgment` GREATER THAN 45
    AND (NOT `exceptional circumstances`)
    AND (NOT `disposed of under section 15`)

-- s 19(2): "The Registrar must, within 7 days of the making of the determination or order, send certified copies ... to the
-- applicant and the relevant contracting authority."
GIVEN `days after the determination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certified copies were sent in time` IF
    `days after the determination` AT MOST 7

§§ `18(3), (5) and 21(1) -- what the applicant can win`

-- s 18(3): if the determination is in the applicant's favour the Tribunal may "(a) order any decision or action ... to be set
-- aside; (b) order the contracting authority to make a decision or take action ... in place of that which has been set aside
-- ...; (c) order the contracting authority to amend any document pertaining to the procurement; (d) order the contracting
-- authority to pay to the applicant the costs of participation in the qualification of suppliers, or the costs of tender
-- preparation, reasonably incurred". (5): "Despite subsection (3), if -- (a) the Tribunal makes a determination in favour of the
-- applicant; and (b) the contract for the procurement has already been awarded, the Tribunal may only -- (c) make an order under
-- subsection (3)(d); or (d) if the applicant did not incur any of the costs mentioned in subsection (3)(d), award the applicant
-- the costs of the challenge proceeding in accordance with section 21."
-- s 21(1): "the costs of any challenge proceeding ... are at the discretion of the Tribunal."
-- No remedy anywhere in the Act is damages for the lost contract (lost profit); the most is tender or qualification costs.
-- Reading: where the contract is not yet awarded, the s 21(1) discretion is read as open; where it is awarded and the applicant
-- did incur (3)(d) costs, s 18(5) is read literally as shutting out challenge-proceeding costs. A determination against the
-- applicant is not modelled for costs (s 21 is a general discretion); every s 18(3) remedy is then unavailable.
DECLARE Remedy IS ONE OF
    `setting aside the decision`
    `ordering a decision in its place`
    `amending a procurement document`
    `tender or qualification costs`
    `costs of the challenge proceeding`

GIVEN `the remedy` IS A Remedy, `contract already awarded` IS A BOOLEAN, `applicant incurred tender or qualification costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may give a successful applicant` IF
    CONSIDER `the remedy`
    WHEN `tender or qualification costs` THEN `applicant incurred tender or qualification costs`
    WHEN `costs of the challenge proceeding` THEN
        (NOT `contract already awarded`) OR (NOT `applicant incurred tender or qualification costs`)
    OTHERWISE NOT `contract already awarded`

§§ `24 -- keeping the documents`

-- s 24: "A contracting authority must ensure that all documents relating to procurements subject to this Act are retained for a
-- minimum of 3 years from the date of their creation."
GIVEN `months since creation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authority may now discard the document` IF
    `months since creation` AT LEAST 36
